{
  "_comment": [
    "Model panel for the expanded memorization screening.",
    "release: OpenRouter 'created' date (UTC), fetched 2026-07-26 from https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models.",
    "price_in / price_out: USD per 1e6 tokens at the same date. Used by estimate_cost.py.",
    "reasoning: value passed to ask_gpt_threaded(reasoning_effort=...). 'none' where the provider",
    "  permits fully disabling deliberation; 'max_tokens:128' or 'minimal' for endpoints that reject it.",
    "corpus: 'open' means the pre-training corpus is publicly documented and n-gram-searchable",
    "  (only OLMo 3, via infini-gram over OLMo-mix / Dolma). 'weights' means open weights, closed data.",
    "in_prior_study: audited in the 13-model version of this paper (results/ already contains these cells).",
    "service_tier: 'flex' where OpenRouter actually exposes a flex endpoint (verified against /api/v1/models/<id>/endpoints on 2026-07-26, cached in results/meta/flex_support.json). Only Google (6) and OpenAI terra/luna/sol/5.5 have one; each is exactly 50% of standard, and price_in/price_out below are the flex prices for those. Anthropic exposes no flex endpoint at all -- the claude_*_flex entries in the LLM library (src/lib/LLMs.jl) are therefore billed at standard rates despite the name. xAI offers priority only.",
    "providers: routing order required to reach the flex endpoint. Empty means default routing.",
    "reasoning: chosen by MEASUREMENT, not assumption (src/calibrate_reasoning.py, results/meta/reasoning_calibration.json, 2026-07-26). reasoning={max_tokens:128} is ignored by several endpoints -- Gemini 3.1 Pro emitted 641 tokens when asked for 128, Gemini 3 Flash 765, and GPT-5.5 burned all 800 and returned an empty answer, losing 24% of its pilot calls. The setting recorded here is the one that actually minimised emitted reasoning tokens while still returning a parseable number; reasoning_tokens_measured is what it actually emitted."
  ],
